{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-06T20:51:26.186Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1c3d835edba106c1302b3106","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.291","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-rust-rnex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Install the published-CLI oracle from a committed lockfile in CI"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"CI installs the conformance oracle with npm install -g @unbrained/pm-cli@<pin> and npm exec --package=..., pinning only the top-level package. The CLI ships no shrinkwrap (unbraind/pm-cli#1417), so a partially propagated OpenTelemetry 2.12.0 release failed all six runners in run 37472610207 (pm-rust-otel). Commit tests/oracle/package.json + package-lock.json, install with npm ci --prefix tests/oracle on Linux/macOS/Windows, point PM_NODE_CLI and the merge-driver/health steps at that install, update tests/release_pipeline_contract.rs pins, and let Dependabot (npm, /tests/oracle) bump it. Raised by CodeRabbit on PR #60 (comment 4200300693, zizmor adhoc-packages)."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Task"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["ci","reproducibility","upstream"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-06T20:51:26.186Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-06T20:51:26.186Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"claude-orchestrator"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Every CI job installs the oracle via npm ci from a committed lockfile; zizmor